            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Vien Brauhaus",
            "review_text": "Liam E\n1 contribution\n0\nBest Beer in Hanoi\nDec 2018 • Family\nFor the few, still surviving beer drinkers out there, this is the place for good value, high quality beer. It also serves excellent Czech and Vietnamese food.\n\nIt seems that the traditional, north European enjoyment of good food and beer is a dying culture, but it kept alive in Vietnam by the Hoa Vien breweries and restaurants, and the Vietnamese people themselves. Don’t let the noise put you off, that’s just an indication of a good restaurant in Vietnam, just as it is in Chinese culture.\n\nThe beer is brewed on the premises and is every but as good as Czech beer in the Czech Republic; it should be, it the breweries were built by the Czechs who then trained the Vietnamese brewers, and trained them very well. And considering the prices for beer in some of the restaurants in Hanoi, it is definitely the best value in Hanoi.\n\nThere are 2 outlets in Hanoi, the main brew house at 1A Tang Bat Ho, and a smaller but just as nice place at 10 Nguyen Bieu. Enjoy, if you are a genuine beer enthusiast.\n\nIt's a pity about Tripadvisor restrictions on 'What sort of visit?' The place is good for couples, family, friends, business and solo.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 19, 2018",
