            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Vien Brauhaus",
            "review_text": "Micky_D_S6\nSheffield, United Kingdom98 contributions\n0\nGreat beer, good atmosphere\nNov 2017 • Couples\nWe ate here on our first night in Vietnam and made our choice based on the fact that it was near to our hotel.\nWe visited on a busy Saturday night and were unable to get an outside table. The staff offered us an upstairs balcony table but the humidity up there was unbearable; fans were located around the ground floor outside tables.\nOnce we settled inside staff brought beer menus and were very helpful as we were making our choices for food. Food is traditional Vietnamese, slightly more expensive than places we ate at on subsequent evenings, with big portions. We had a starter of spring rolls to share, a plate of bamboo shoots and veg, and a noodle dish each. We would have had enough food without the starter or with just one noodle dish between us.\nAll in all an enjoyable evening, although not traditionally Vietnamese, with plenty of good beer and decent food.\nRead more\nWritten November 15, 2017",
